A||||21||80's BOY||Why didn't this work????||||5||
Z||000000||80's BOY||07-06-2000||02:56 PM||||installed the stang 19# injectors AND the pressure regulator. cranked it up and it sounded really cool. got in, and it's DEAD off the line. pressure's 55 at the rail so i weened it to 45 and still the same results. after a few minutes it wasn't even streetable. i limped home and re-installed the factory injectors but increased the pressure up to about 50. i can tell a little hp increase, but would still like to use the larger injectors. what did i do wrong?? should i re-install the larger injectors and start at a lower pressure?? any ideas are appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||80's BOY||07-06-2000||02:58 PM||||forgot to mention the engine....a HIGHLY modified, naturally aspirated 3.1 stroker with resonated freeflow exhaust.many mods.||||reg||2
Z||000002||terryk||07-06-2000||03:50 PM||||Because more fuel is not always the answer.<P>To correctly do what you are attempting, you need a scanner to read the BLM, INT, and O2 readings.<P>You have no way of knowing the mixture or the ECM's view of the world. You threw in bigger injectors and cranked up the FP. Since the ECM tries to set the power enrichment AFR to 12:1 (which is god-awful rich as it is), you just made it even worse. <P>With stock injectors, FP and ECM calibrations your mods probibly leaned it out more in the right direction. You may have just taken a step backwards.||||reg||4
Z||000003||BBBAD GT||07-06-2000||04:15 PM||||I agree with terryk.  Cranking up the FP to 50 psi with 19lb injectors is making them feel like they are around 24lb injectors.  <P>Doing the math, if you have BSFC at .50, and 16lb injectors, you can make max. about 210 hp with stock fuel pressure at 39 psi(is that what the Fiero is?).  Now, if you crank up the FP to approx 45 psi, then your 16lb inj are acting like approx 19lb injectors which can support around 240 hp.  Of course, this is just pushing numbers, and the real world can be a bit different, but you get the idea.<P>Getting your correct A/F ratio seems like a shot in the dark.  WOT mixture might be easy to pin point, but your driveability will be the hardest to accomplish.  Good luck.<P>Sure wish the Fieros has Mass Air, makes life a whole lot simpler when upgrading injectors.<P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||80's BOY||07-06-2000||05:40 PM||||i did the math, guys. i came up with needing about 18# on my injectors so that's why i chose the stang injectors. i then increased my FP to match the increased demand on the rail. maybe i need a piggyback unit on my ECM. as it is, i used 180hp as an estimate but still no dyno runs available. surely with the huge overbore, port and polish along with exhaust mods and intake alterations thre should be plenty room for play. not just non-streetable results. besides, what happens when you buy high performance injectors say from the Fiero Store?? how does that differ??||||reg||4
Z||000005||Cooter||07-06-2000||09:26 PM||||In the for what it's worth department: The very nice man who is working with me on a chip for my 3.4 has sent two- one is leaner at WOT than the factory chip, the second is even leaner than the first. After running and timing the cars acceleration with all three chips, the leanest one has produced the quickest acceleration times. <BR>Please don't ask who is making my chip. If he wants you to know who he is, he will find you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||80's BOY||07-06-2000||09:41 PM||||please send him my direction. i consider my little stroker an "above average" project and would like to get the full potential of the buildup.||||reg||7
Z||000007||terryk||07-06-2000||10:05 PM||||Grassy Knoll.....<P>Again, you're tuning in the dark. It's logical that you need more fuel, but you've gone way overboard. Add to this the fact that GM tends to run the engines rich since there is no way to know the AFR at WOT. <P>The increase in displacement is minor. The "free flowing" stuff is good, but it doesn't require that much additional fuel.<P>You need some way of determining the current state of the ECM. At least get a digital voltmeter and look at the O2 during WOT. Back off the fuel pressure down to the 40-45PSI range so they don't spit. See how it does then.<P>Also, injectors are very hard to control at low pulse widths. That's why there is a correction in the ECM. Going to larger injectors just makes it worse. Idle and low RPM driveability can go all to hell. The smallest injector that works seems to be the best. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||BBBAD GT||07-07-2000||12:05 AM||||I agree that the smallest injector you can get away with is probably your best bet. <P>If only the EEC knew how much air your motor is getting at all rpms, life would be alot simpler.  <P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||07-07-2000||02:16 AM||||Why BBBad, you brought up an interesting point...<P>The 85 2.8L MPFI engine used in the W engine Celebrity/X-11 or S engine Camaro is the same engine as the Fiero 9 engine.  <P>The only difference (other than physical changes to make them fit), is that the Fiero is Speed Density with a MAP and the Celebrity is Mass Air flow with a Mass Air Flow sensor (clever how that works). <P>Both were certified at the same time as backup's to each other should one fail Federal/California certification. Both passed. The Rochester vs Holley TB and top plenum is the other difference.<P>Now then the ECM's: The 1226869/7170 (Fiero)is essentially the same circuitry as the 1226870. The only real difference is the internal processor code. In fact, if you compare the wiring, there is only a few subtle changes. Very little difference. The Vette made use of the ESC knock sensor and air pump whereas the V6's didn't. <P>Ergo, find a 1226870 ECM from an 85 W engine Celebrity/X-11/Olds Ciera or Corvette. Buy/steal/find an 85 manual or automatic transmission eprom (Camaro 2.8L manual trans is a good source or ADS. Of course most Celebrities were automatics), get the mass and mass relay from the Celebrity/X-11, install the ECM and mass/relay, add a few wires, and tada you have a Mass Air Flow system. <P>You can leave the MAP in place and with little effort, switch back and forth.<P>No, the Fiero eprom will not work in the 1226870 ECM and vice-versa.<P>Terry<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||80's BOY||07-07-2000||09:28 AM||||then why do people spend $400 on a set of performance injectors?? do they even help??||||reg||5
Z||000011||pollock||07-07-2000||09:50 AM||||Awesome! a fiero with Mass Air!!<P>Terry clearly knows his stuff here. (or he's baffling me with BS, hehe) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I personally do not know my stuff here, but i do know that 5.0 Mustangs became much better from the '89 Speed Density cars to the '90 Mass Air cars, and the conversion for the earlier ones is a very hot swap.  It responds SO much better to changes.<P>I think it's time i hit the junkyard<P>HELL YEAH!||||reg||14
Z||000012||BBBAD GT||07-07-2000||10:46 AM||||The 5.0 conversion to MAF is a very simple swap.  This would be a great project for somebody to persue with a Fiero (hint hint). <P>If you spend the money on bigger injectors, you get just that, bigger squirters.  Nothing is said how the EEC will control them.  I'd say if you increased your airflow to the motor X%, then you should increase your injector the same or near the same % so the Fiero EEC would still produce the same a/f mixture ratio as before, and would still think its controlling stock airflow/injectors (looks like you have done just that 80's boy).   Like I said, its difficult to do just that because of so many factors.  It looks like its trial/error time without mass air.<P><P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||80's BOY||07-07-2000||10:55 AM||||trial and error SUCKS!! i'll bet i can pull off the plenum and fuel rails in my sleep after this.||||reg||8
Z||000014||terryk||07-07-2000||12:17 PM||||I've had both engines. Fiero SD seems to handle changes pretty good unless the vacuum is really bad. I noticed that a high overlap cam in the X-11 wasn't received very well by the mass. Also, masses are more expensive than maps but the PNP's are full of them now. I'd do the conversion only if you are curious or have made some really wild changes.<P>Good quesion. Why do people install high performance injectors? (it's rhetorical). More air, more fuel. <P>I understand that adding bigger injection and raising the FP is the only option when the base injector pulse width can't be increased via the ECM.<P>Again, to do it right, get a scanner.<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||BBBAD GT||07-07-2000||12:58 PM||||Funny you ask.  With the Mustang, I've had 19lb injectors stock, upgraded to 24lb when I did heads and cam, upgraded to 30lb when the blower went on, and now I have 36lb when I upgraded the blower.  I have 47lb inj waiting to put on, so I wouldn't have to rely on increased fuel pressure so much.  <P>Simply need more fuel.<P>BTW, I've seen 77lb injectors idle like a kitten at 800 rpm's on a blown stang before (of course, it was electronically tuned).<P>IMO, for a Fiero seeing less than 200 hp, I really don't see a need for bigger injectors over the 16lb units. <BR><P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Alex4mula||07-07-2000||01:22 PM||||Up to now I agree with BAD. My new 3.4 has K&N, bored/ported everything from TBS to lower plenum and FOCOA headers. More air will go in only with SC or Turbo or maybe porting heads. I'm using my stock 2.8 injectors and the car is running very rich (AutoXray scanner reading). Still trying tunning that. Don't see need for bigger injectors still. Why something less than that will need them?||||reg||12
